claim.claim-text:
a screw shaft (38) that is connected to a brake cable (37) ;
an actuator case (39) that supports the screw shaft (38) movably in an axial direction thereof;
an electric motor (40) that is supported by the actuator case (39) rotatably forward and backward;
a motion conversion mechanism (41) that has a nut (61) to be screwed onto the screw shaft (38), enables conversion from a rotational motion generated in the electric motor (40) to a linear motion of the screw shaft (38), and is accommodated in the actuator case (39); and
a rotation restricting means (73) that restricts a rotational motion of the screw shaft (38), wherein switching between pulling the brake cable (37) and loosening the brake cable (37) is performed by a change in a rotational direction of the electric motor (40),
wherein the brake cable (37) is formed by twisting a plurality of wires (92), the direction of twisting is rotational direction of the nut (61) when the brake cable (37) is pulled.
